00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:09,140
Slide 4 dissects THE TROJAN HORSE: Google App for Windows. James, why do we call this innocent search bar a Trojan Horse?

2
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:13,921
Because it disguises deep system capture as a harmless utility!

3
00:00:13,921 --> 00:00:17,120
Look at the three hidden objectives on screen:

4
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,591
Objective 1: Hotkey Hijacking.

5
00:00:19,591 --> 00:00:27,530
By seizing `Alt + Space`, Google catches your mental search intent before you ever touch Windows Search or Copilot!

6
00:00:27,930 --> 00:00:30,673
Objective 2: Perpetual Memory Residency!

7
00:00:30,673 --> 00:00:40,070
It configures itself in Windows Startup registry, keeping an entire Chromium instance alive in RAM 24/7 so it pops up in 20 milliseconds!

8
00:00:40,470 --> 00:00:44,377
And Objective 3 is the most aggressive: Screen Vision Portal!

9
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:54,370
It puts Google Lens directly on your desktop, allowing one-click capture of every pixel on your screen—including confidential spreadsheets and private code!

10
00:00:54,770 --> 00:01:01,440
You think you installed a calculator search bar, but you actually installed a 24/7 screen surveillance portal!

11
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:09,280
When you install a Trojan Horse, you are trading your system resources and visual privacy for fractional convenience.

